    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113-a4">

                <pb facs="0279" n="207" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg207"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 331.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr.
                            Fogarty</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1881-03-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 8, 1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 6th of March, inquiring what my course would be in case
                    you should be arrested under the coercion act; I have to say in reply that
                    whenever such a contingency should arise, and I should be consulted on the
                    subject, I would give to it my best consideration, and do whatever my duty might
                    require. It would be manifestly improper for me to express any opinion upon a
                    hypothetical case.</p>
                <p>I am,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
